From 60fa608fb8a16bbbf6322a07d3ba8a753b1a240a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Alonso <nick@drkm.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:04:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Inkling: use RotatingKVCache for the sliding layers,
 drop the shifting caches

A decode microbenchmark (bench/K2/cache_bench.py) put the in-place rotating
cache at or slightly ahead of the shifting designs, so the sliding layers use
RotatingKVCache and BatchRotatingKVCache. The relative bias of a single
token is gathered with one slot-to-distance index per forward, provided by
the new RotatingKVCache.key_distances(); the bias bank is stored reversed so
the global layers slice it without a flip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
